sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 25-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite (referee re-score) — MorphoEval overall 26.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Independent referee re-score of the 25-law `@drmichaellevin` synthesis suite: 26.4/100 (v1 self-score 93.8), verdict band 'unfaithful'. The v1 audit's evidence loci belong to the superseded 6-law script, so the 25-law rewrite had never been examined. On examination: 2 of 25 Python laws compute anything (Law 7 secretary sum, Law 8 truth table), 1 fits its own generating function (Law 5), 16 evaluate one closed-form expression at one hard-coded point with `ref` set to the same expression, and 6 are literals or tautologies (Laws 6, 9, 10, 17, 19, 24); no ODE/PDE/SDE/Markov/NCA system named in any title is integrated. In Lean, 2 theorems are genuine exhaustive Bool proofs (Laws 8, 10), 10 pair a trivially-universal identity with ground constants, 13 are entirely ground `decide` arithmetic, and Law 7's theorem brackets a rigged constant (100566 = 37 x 2718). Nothing empirical is loaded: the script no longer reads `levin_youtube_catalog.json` (still declared as an input in the math-KG YAML and as a 'specimen' in v1), the catalog's law mapping is the stale 6-law taxonomy, and all 25 v1 measurements reference the suite's own Lean theorem with `reference_value == value` for 23. The bibliography covers 6 of 25 laws, and Crossref resolution shows a title/DOI mismatch (`froese2024`), a wrong article number (`pigozzi2025` 1112 vs 1027), a fabricated title (`biswas2023`) and a mis-transcribed title (`chvykov2021`). Four C5 tags have no pre-registration artefact; Laws 16, 21 and 22 are O1-tagged scalar reductions; Law 7's O1 attribution to Froese is unsupported by either Froese paper's abstract; the docs' tier counts (T2 8/25, T4 8/25) disagree with the table and script (9, 7). The CLI exposes only `--self-test`. `--self-test` passes (0.3 s) and both Lean modules compile with 0 sorry; `--conform` on the v1 audit passes, which shows the schema check cannot catch stale loci or tautological measurements. Overall 26.4/100 (faithfulness 18.7, reproducibility 44.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit bfe377c2; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 36, Morphological realism / specimen match 10, Parameter expressivity 22, Morphometric validation 8, Source and data traceability 35, Code-to-model traceability 44, Reproducibility package 52. Output judged: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png: rendered output of models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted). Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cf19761e9e6760d1e706dce6a8fdea337079e70d318494d21ee724915d6bb697; artifact_sha256: 2e2cd28df81d42a235a6c03f640c7a351859e4a4f758ee4692323ad541edbfaa; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json=38aab3be23160a82..., datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib=5acabab1711c1899...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive-light-cone framework (diagrammatic, no closed-form R_eff(N, G_gj) is published) | Chvykov et al. (2021) Science 371:90: low-rattling stationary measure P_ss(x) ~ r(x)^(-gamma) tested on robotic 'smarticle' collectives | Bongard & Levin (2023) Biomimetics 8:110: polycomputing as a conceptual framework (no XOR/AND/OR state-map equation is published) | Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025) Commun. Biol. 8:1027: associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models; Watson & Szathmary (2016) TREE 31:147: natural induction / Hebbian attractor deepening | Rosas et al. (2019) Phys. Rev. E 100:032305: O-information Omega(X^n); Scheibner et al. (2020) / Tan et al. (2022): odd elasticity and chiral crystal work cycles; Gilbert & Mosteller (1966): the 1/e secretary-problem law | Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; Cervera, Levin & Mafe: voltage-gated gap-junction bistability (cited in the KG without DOI); reconstructed_in_script: 25 scalar quantities evaluated once each at hard-coded constants (L49-L200); a 24-state power-law table and its own log-log fit (Law 5, L72-L77); a 99-term secretary-problem sum (Law 7, L84-L89); a 4-row x 3-gate truth table (Law 8, L91-L96) | A `laws_summary` list (L202-L228) assigning each law an `equation_origin` (O1/O2), an `epistemic_tier` (T1-T4), a `criteria_passed` list (C1-C5), video IDs, the computed `metric` and a `ref` that is, for 23 of 25 laws, the same expression or its rounded value | An 8-panel figure (L244-L377) whose panels 5, 6 and 8 plot analytic decoration curves (10 exp(-0.8 t), a piecewise sine for ln|S|, exp(-0.4 t), 0.5^(t/2), exp(-0.6 t) cos(1.2 t)) that are not produced by any computation in verify_all_25_laws() | 25 Lean 4 theorems in Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean (0 sorry; 2 exhaustive Bool proofs, 10 trivially-universal identities paired with ground constants, 13 ground `decide` checks); 6 earlier theorems in MathOfBiology.lean section 16; transfer_boundary: Every dynamical law in the titles (Cervera gap-junction ODE, Nernst-Planck PDE, Chvykov Markov jump process, Brenner Langevin SDE, Friston gradient flow, Weinberg Ca2+ integral-feedback ODE, Rebbin cable equation, Guichard NCA) is replaced by a single algebraic consequence evaluated at one point; none is integrated, so no regime, bifurcation, threshold or breakdown horizon (criterion C4) is actually exhibited | The S_6 causal-emergence numbers in Law 17 (0.8687, 0.0191, 1.0000, 0.0313, 0.7209, 0.1238) are copied from the repository's own earlier sorting-morphogenesis run (sorting-morphogenesis/PLATONIC_SPACE_CLAIMS_EVALUATION.md L112-L118), not recomputed and not from Hoel (2026) | Law 5's slope of -1.0000 is guaranteed by construction (p_ss is defined as r_exit^-1 / Z at L75); it tests numpy.polyfit, not Chvykov's law | Law 7's Python optimum (k* = 37, P = 0.37104) is the classical secretary problem; its Lean theorem brackets 100566 = 37 x 2718 rather than 100 x 1000 (floor(100000/2718) = 36), so the machine-checked statement is not floor(N/e) = 37 | Law 16's Python metric (Shannon-Hartley capacity 2.0 bits at SNR 15, L136-L139) and its Lean theorem (E_total - E_maint - E_info = 30, Loop L251-L258) are different equations; the measurement sidecar reports the former under the latter's theorem name | The video catalog is metadata only (titles, durations, views, descriptions, a stale 6-law `mappedMathLaws` field); no transcript, slide or figure text is parsed, so 'extracted from the channel' is a manual attribution, not a reproducible extraction; does_not_claim: This referee audit does not claim any of the 25 source equations is wrong as published; it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates them, and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C5 tags are earned by the artefacts | It does not verify the content of the 72 referenced videos (no transcripts are available offline) and does not re-derive the S_6 causal-emergence numbers | It does not claim the Lean modules fail: both compile with 0 sorry; the finding is about what the theorems state, not whether they check." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Commit the 25-law script, Lean loop, YAML, docs and KG payload so a checkpoint commit exists, re-run the v1 assessor's audit against that commit with evidence loci that resolve, and in the figure / KG replace 'Lean 4 Kernel Verified' with a per-law tag (structural / ground) so readers can see which 2 of 25 theorems quantify over anything.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib and the audit references - correct `froese2024` (split into Entropy 25(5):748 (2023, DOI 10.3390/e25050748) and Entropy 26(4):288 (2024, 'Irruption and Absorption')), `pigozzi2025` (article 1027), `biswas2023` (title of record for 10.3390/ijms24010285), `chvykov2021` ('active collectives'); add DOIs / arXiv ids for the 17 laws with no bib entry (Pietak 2016 10.3389/fbioe.2016.00055 and 2017 10.1098/rsif.2017.0425; Rosas 2019 10.1103/PhysRevE.100.032305; Tan 2022 10.1038/s41586-022-04889-6; Scheibner 2020 10.1038/s41567-020-0795-y; Liu 2024 arXiv:2404.19756; Ororbia & Friston arXiv:2311.09589; Guichard & Nichele arXiv:2504.11855; Cervera-Levin-Mafe 2021; Hoel 2026 Patterns; Bode 1945; Kolmogorov 1957; Weinberg 2025; Pezzulo & Levin 2015; Friston 2010/2013), each with a note on whether the DOI was resolved.",
            "remediation needed: docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md:56-82, models/...py:202-228 and docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json - retag: Law 7 O1 -> O2 with the attribution corrected to Lindley (1961) / Gilbert & Mosteller (1966) and the Froese link described as 'discussed in', not 'published equation'; Laws 16, 21, 22 O1 -> O2 (budget identity, diagonal 2-component proxy for the Fisher flow, scalar (K12 - K21) * Area in place of the odd modulus cycle integral); remove C5 from Laws 3, 5, 17, 22 until a hash-locked pre-registered held-out test exists for each in this repository and is linked; demote Law 24 (T3 'cross-clade empirical') and Law 23 (T2 'validated in wet-lab') to T4 until an empirical comparison exists; reconcile the section 3 tier counts (T2 9, T4 7) with the table. Implement or delete the Huxley allometry half of Law 22 (alpha = 1.42 is dead code at L180 with no source).",
            "remediation needed: models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py:202-228 - for every law set `ref` to a value that does not come from the same expression: a published number with its citation and uncertainty (e.g. Chvykov 2021 measured enrichment, Pigozzi 2025 conditioning success rate, Tan 2022 chiral-crystal rotation rate), or state `ref: null` and label the entry 'internal consistency'. Fix Law 3's 4.7002 -> 4.6992 and Law 20's 'dominates at k = 16' -> 'k >= 17' (pi_C(16) = pi_D(16)). Lower the assert tolerance at L384 to a relative 1e-6 for analytic identities.",
            "remediation needed: models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py:398-403 - expose the model constants on the CLI (--n-cells, --g-half, --v-th, --v0, --delta-v-mv, --peclet, --gamma, --n-states, --eta, --n-genes, --kappa, --snr, --b, --c, --g-eph, --rho, --law to select a subset, --no-figure, --out-dir) and make --self-test exercise render_25_laws_atlas() into a temporary directory without writing into morphoeval/runs/.",
            "remediation needed: models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py:49-200 - replace the 22 one-point / literal evaluations with the dynamical object each law names and compute the law as an output, not an input: integrate the Cervera gap-junction ODE on a 2-cell / 1-D chain and show the depolarised-domain isolation (Law 2); solve the 1-D Nernst-Planck steady state numerically and recover exp(-zF dV/RT) with G_gj swept (Law 3); build a 24-state driven Markov chain with heterogeneous exit rates, compute its stationary vector, then fit the exponent (Law 5); instantiate the 3-clause 3-SAT energy and evaluate it on all 8 assignments (Law 10); run the Hopfield / GRN Hebbian update on an N = 16 network and measure Delta E (Laws 11-12); simulate the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck SDE and measure the stationary variance (Law 13); integrate the Ca2+ integral-feedback ODE with saturation and locate the bifurcation (Law 24); run a minimal NCA and measure the contraction factor (Law 25); compute Omega from the XOR joint distribution (Law 18); evaluate a concrete S(iw) and integrate ln|S| numerically (Law 19). Delete the literals at L106, L158-L159, L191-L192.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean:113-119 - Law 7: replace N_scaled = 100566 with a statement that is actually true of floor(N/e) (e.g. prove 36 * 2718 <= 100000 < 37 * 2718, i.e. floor(100/e) = 36, and separately state that the discrete optimum is k* = 37 via the computed objective), or drop the floor(N/e) claim; the current theorem checks a constant chosen to make it hold.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_levin_youtube_channel_math.lean:90-93, 194-258, 271-287, 316-334, 364-394 - replace the 13 ground `decide` theorems with universally quantified statements of the laws they name: e.g. (Law 5) for all p1 p2 r1 r2, p1 * r1 = p2 * r2 -> r1 < r2 -> p1 > p2; (Law 15) for all e p h, h < p -> ...; (Law 21) for all g11 g22 d1 d2 : Int, 0 < g11 -> 0 < g22 -> 0 <= g11 d1^2 + g22 d2^2; (Law 23) for all g d, 0 < g -> d != 0 -> -2 g d^2 < 0; (Law 25) for all n, e / 2^n <= e with strict decrease for e > 0; (Law 16) prove the equation the Python computes or change the Python to the budget identity. Remove the hard-coded `all_lean4_verified: True` at L232 and have run_all() invoke `lean` (or read a lake build artefact) so the flag is measured.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml - refresh the 19 drifted `code_locus` ranges (Laws 1-12, 19-25) to the current file and add a CI check (the loop validator) that fails when a locus no longer contains the law's comment header.",
            "remediation needed: morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml:7-8 and datasets/levin_youtube_channel/ - either have the script load levin_youtube_catalog.json, verify SHA-256 38aab3be23160a82403c57ccb5f9b6f6cca81519b4d10444dd4f20f530acf2d3, and derive something from it (at minimum check that every cited video ID exists and regenerate `mappedMathLaws` from the 25-law table), or remove it from `inputs`. Update `mappedMathLaws` from the 6-law taxonomy to the 25-law ids, rewrite README.md ('6 governing mathematical laws') for the 25-law suite, record the catalog hash in the README, and commit the crawl script so the 374-video inventory is reproducible." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.264"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 2)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

